  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569223.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Fish Catch Data from the Central Bering Sea and Gulf of Alaska Sampled by the R/V Kaiyo maru during the Summer and Fall 2003",
  "description": "Salmon and pelagic nekton catch data were collected in the central Bering Sea and Gulf of Alaska by the Japanese R/V Kaiyo maru from June to September 2003. A pelagic rope trawl that was towed with the headrope at the surface (0 m; 1 hr at 3.5-5.0 knots) was used to sample 61 stations. Salmon catch data includes chum and sockeye salmon.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect fish as part of the BASIS survey of the Bering Sea.",
